@@ -992,6 +992,28 @@ to FALSE to retain the historical diagnostic mapping from layers 3--4 liquid
 volumetric water content to moss water content.
 </entry>
 
+<entry id="use_moss_topsoil_ice_limitation" type="logical" category="physics"
+       group="elm_inparm" valid_values="" value=".false.">
+Experimental peatland moss photosynthesis sensitivity. Scale the moss
+tissue-water photosynthesis factor by the liquid fraction of water in the top
+soil layer, SOILLIQ/(SOILLIQ+SOILICE). This is an instantaneous proxy for
+capitulum thaw, not a prognostic moss ice store; it does not freeze or thaw
+water in the moss mass or alter the energy budget. Defaults to TRUE when
+use_humhol is enabled and FALSE otherwise; an explicit setting takes priority.
+</entry>
+
+<entry id="use_moss_separate_respiration_stress" type="logical" category="physics"
+       group="elm_inparm" valid_values="" value=".false.">
+Experimental peatland moss leaf-respiration moisture response. If TRUE,
+calculate leaf maintenance respiration stress separately from the
+photosynthesis/VPD response, using moss_leaf_mr_dry_fraction and
+moss_leaf_mr_full_water_content from the parameter file. Fine-root
+maintenance respiration is unchanged. With topsoil ice limitation enabled,
+the separate leaf response is also scaled by the topsoil liquid fraction.
+Defaults to TRUE when use_humhol is enabled and FALSE otherwise; set FALSE
+explicitly to retain the previous shared-scalar behavior.
+</entry>
+
 <entry id="use_peatland_vertical_transport" type="logical" category="physics"
        group="elm_inparm" valid_values="" value=".false.">
 If TRUE, peat-bearing topounits use peat-specific vertical transport
